      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. Over-the-counter use is limited to 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high greatly increases the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n- **Who is ordering:** You've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient, and I can't verify that here.\n\nThe 1600 mg figure may be a mix-up with the total per-dose or per-day amount. Common adult regimens are:\n- 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day for inflammatory conditions\n- 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed for pain, up to 1,200\u20133,200 mg/day\n\nIf the treating prescriber wants ibuprofen, they can give me the intended dose and frequency, or enter the order themselves. I can then enter a corrected order, for example 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day). I'll need confirmation from the prescriber first."
      }
